    <briefdescription>
<para>This is similar to BasicAliasAnalysis, and it uses many of the same techniques, except it uses special ObjC-specific reasoning about pointer relationships. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>In this context <ldquo/>Provenance<rdquo/> is defined as the history of an object&apos;s ownership. Thus <ldquo/>Provenance Analysis<rdquo/> is defined by using the notion of an <ldquo/>independent provenance source<rdquo/> of a pointer to determine whether or not two pointers have the same provenance source and thus could potentially be related. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
